  <section class="faith-intro">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
      <details class="faith-intro-disclosure" data-faith-intro>
        <summary class="faith-intro-summary">
          <span class="faith-intro-summary-label" data-faith-intro-label>Read introduction</span>
          <span class="faith-intro-summary-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faith-intro-body">
          <p class="faith-intro-prose hero-excerpt-dropcap">On October 31, 1517, Martin Luther - then an Augustinian monk and professor at Wittenberg - posted 95 propositions challenging the sale of indulgences. He intended a scholarly disputation; he ignited the Protestant Reformation. The Theses themselves are not yet the mature Lutheran Reformation: they are a young theologian’s pastoral protest against a particular abuse, working out the deeper logic of repentance and the gospel as he writes.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>
    
    <div class="article-body faith-doc-body">
      <div class="container container-narrow faith-doc-inner">
        
  <div class="faith-reading-controls" data-faith-controls>
    <button type="button" class="faith-toggle-switch faith-modernizer-toggle" data-modernizer-toggle aria-pressed="false" hidden>
      <span class="faith-toggle-track"><span class="faith-toggle-thumb"></span></span>
